"The 'Amazing Box' aka Mandbox formula, invented by TGlad at fractalforums.com.\n\nThe formula for one iteration looks like this:\n\nx = abs(x+Fold) - abs(x-Fold) - x\ny = abs(y+Fold) - abs(y-Fold) - y\nz = abs(z+Fold) - abs(z-Fold) - z\nrr = x*x + y*y + z*z\nif rr < sqr(Min_R) then m = Scale/sqr(Min_R) else\nif rr < 1 then m = Scale/rr else m = Scale\nx = x * m + Cx\ny = y * m + Cy\nz = z * m + Cz" = "La formula 'Amazing Box' alias Mandbox, inventata da TGlad su fractalforums.com.\n\nLa formula per un'iterazione si presenta così:\n\nx = abs(x+Fold) - abs(x-Fold) - x\ny = abs(y+Fold) - abs(y-Fold) - y\nz = abs(z+Fold) - abs(z-Fold) - z\nrr = x*x + y*y + z*z\nif rr < sqr(Min_R) then m = Scale/sqr(Min_R) else\nif rr < 1 then m = Scale/rr else m = Scale\nx = x * m + Cx\ny = y * m + Cy\nz = z * m + Cz";
"The camera goes once around the object." = "La fotocamera fa un giro completo intorno all’oggetto.";
